1
00:00:10,622 --> 00:00:17,124
Everybody here holds a role, and the list
says which. That, and not their job title,

2
00:00:17,124 --> 00:00:19,910
is what decides what they can reach.

3
00:00:20,365 --> 00:00:26,356
Here they all are. Each one says how
much it grants and how many people hold it.

4
00:00:26,809 --> 00:00:32,150
Some came with the product. Those you
can copy and adjust, but not break.

5
00:00:32,604 --> 00:00:38,394
Open one and it is a plain list, grouped
by the part of the business it touches.

6
00:00:38,394 --> 00:00:40,638
Nothing clever, nothing hidden.

7
00:00:41,091 --> 00:00:47,827
Give it one more thing, and everybody
holding that role has it — without touching a

8
00:00:47,827 --> 00:00:49,775
single person's account.

9
00:00:50,228 --> 00:00:56,445
Or write one of your own, named after a
job you already have. That is the point:

10
00:00:56,445 --> 00:00:58,076
your words, not ours.

11
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:04,856
A role says what somebody may do. Where
they may do it is the workspaces they are

12
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:05,403
put in.

13
00:01:05,856 --> 00:01:10,686
Next: the work itself. Raising a
job, and handing it to somebody.

